\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When, my Saviour, shall I be
\par Perfectly resigned to Thee?
\par Poor and vile in my own eyes,
\par Only in Thy wisdom wise:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Only Thee content to know,
\par Ignorant of all below,
\par Only guided by Thy light,
\par Only mighty in Thy might!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. So I may Thy Spirit know,
\par Let Him as He listeth blow;
\par Let the manner be unknown,
\par So I may with Thee be one.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Fully in my life express
\par All the heights of holiness,
\par Sweetly let my spirit prove
\par All the depths of humble love.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

